src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:366:            Separately, the generic competitor/generic ad group used 18.7% of spend on a small click and conversion sample. Conversion quality for that group total is unverified. The live keyword pull shows it is not a Dynamic Search Ads group: it holds nine static EXACT keywords—six competitor-keyword entries across four competitors plus three generics. Only the sampled government/competitor-query subset was near-zero converting. The evidence gap is therefore whether the group-level reported conversions represent qualified demand and whether the sampled leakage warrants tighter query controls.
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:512:            The next diagnostic pass should retain the resolved Brand cause, the full keyword and match-type pull, the existing negative inventory and the 18.7% generic competitor/generic ad-group finding as starting evidence. It should then reconcile conversion types, downstream qualification, geography, devices, creative, landing pages, settings, bidding history, rank constraints, PMax configuration, remarketing configuration, tracking, consent, target economics and proof permissions.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/open-questions.md:7:| Critical | **Is Meta’s minimum A$600 per 30 days added on top of the existing Search budget, or reallocated from it?** | Search has a mature approximately A$40,000 trailing-12-month history and an observed A$3.0k–A$4.7k monthly range. Reallocation reduces proven demand capture; incremental funding produces a cleaner Meta baseline. | Final choice between Scenario 1 at A$4,246 and preferred Scenario 2 at A$4,846 per 30 days |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/open-questions.md:8:| Critical | **Can PMax receive at least A$50/day—A$1,500 per 30-day planning period—without destabilising Search?** | A 5–10% test slice at the current run-rate does not meet the required floor. PMax must be funded properly or parked. | Scenario 3, PMax relaunch planning and the final channel allocation |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/open-questions.md:9:| Critical | **GO/NO-GO: Does the client approve the free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot as the launch-default offer and dominant CTA, with the adjacent “preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis” caveat in every placement?** | The offer and caveat govern all baseline Search, Meta and landing-page variants. | Campaign copy, creative, form and landing-page launch |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/open-questions.md:12:| Critical | **What exact service geography is approved for the Snapshot and each paid offer, including remote versus onsite limits?** | “Australia-wide” and location-specific messaging cannot be published without confirmed coverage — and the live evidence has sharpened this into a **launch blocker**: the live site commits to **Sydney and Melbourne only**, while the 2026-07-12 search-terms pull spans Canberra, Sydney, Brisbane and national/"near me" terms. The only converting geo-specific term is "ergonomic office fyshwick" (A$250 / 18 clicks / 3 conv at 26% CTR); the Sydney/Melbourne/Brisbane/near-me geo terms appear in the pull but did not convert (`research/live-evidence-2026-07-12.md`). The LP cannot claim broader coverage than the live site until verified; if coverage IS Sydney/Melbourne-only, the Canberra spend needs a geo decision (keep, geo-modify or exclude), not just copy. | Geo targeting, exclusions, landing-page copy, the Appendix A geo-dynamic Canberra treatment, the Appendix B Canberra candidate ad group and lead routing |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/open-questions.md:13:| Critical | **What does ErgoWorks actually issue after training: an accredited certificate, a statement of attainment, participant attendance records, participant training-completion records, or another output?** | Certificate/course buyer type is UNCLASSIFIED, and programme action-status records are not participant credentials. Accreditation and participant-record claims require direct evidence and client sign-off. | Certificate Search test, certificate LP block and FAQ, organisational qualification, final ad copy and publication |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/open-questions.md:14:| Critical | **Are care-sector, online and refresher services actually supported; if so, in what onsite/remote format and approved service geography?** | Keyword demand verifies interest, not delivery capability. The live aged-care/disability/healthcare negatives also conflict with the proposed care build. | Care/online/refresher LP modules, care-sector negative reconciliation, geo labels and targeting, Search creative and publication |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/open-questions.md:16:| Critical | **Do we have admin access to the correct Meta Business Manager, ad account and Dataset/Pixel, plus authority to verify `ergoworksconsulting.com.au` and configure domain verification/AEM?** | Ownership and access are required before an isolated Meta build can be verified or launched. | Meta setup, Pixel/CAPI, domain verification, AEM and launch QA |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/open-questions.md:18:| Critical | **Which CRM is in use, and can it store click IDs, consent records, lead stages and values?** | Google and Meta need reliable offline quality signals so optimisation can move from raw forms toward qualified leads, proposals and won work. | Offline conversion imports, Google Data Manager, Meta CAPI feedback, CPQL reporting and closed-loop attribution |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/open-questions.md:19:| Critical | **What level of separation is approved for Consulting versus Physiotherapy?** Options include campaign-specific goals within the existing Ads account, a dedicated GA4 data stream/property, separate GTM scope, and a separate Meta Pixel/Dataset. | Google Ads account 9258098368 mixes Consulting and Physiotherapy. Health-adjacent data increases privacy and optimisation risk. Separation must not damage the Physiotherapy campaign through account-wide controls. | Conversion cleanup, audience creation, GTM/GA4 architecture, Meta launch, remarketing and reliable reporting |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/open-questions.md:20:| High | **Should paid remarketing receive a separate viable budget after audience creation, or remain parked?** | Remarketing should not share or dilute PMax’s floor. Its value depends on isolated audience size, privacy approval, frequency control and incremental contribution. | Display/Meta retargeting activation, creative volume and audience architecture |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/open-questions.md:21:| High | **How many free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshots can ErgoWorks deliver each week, and who owns response and follow-up?** The Snapshot is preliminary guidance only—**not a compliance assessment, medical assessment, diagnosis or certification**. | Meta may generate uneven lead flow. Slow response or insufficient delivery capacity would damage prospect experience and make channel results difficult to interpret. | Meta pacing, form scheduling, service-area limits, follow-up SLA and scale decisions |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/open-questions.md:22:| High | **Which proof assets are substantiated and approved in writing for paid-media use?** Specifically: reviews and rating, client logos, awards, Danone, and “ASX 100” claims. | These items remain **client sign-off required** and cannot be treated as usable evidence until their accuracy, wording and permissions are confirmed. | Final ad copy, landing-page proof sections, creative production and approval |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/open-questions.md:23:| High | **Is Joel the landing-page developer, what is the delivery window, and where will the page be hosted?** | The dedicated page is a dependency for message match, form design, consent controls, event tracking and paid-traffic routing. | Build schedule, technical specification, launch date, QA ownership and Search/Meta destination mapping |
