docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/D-creative-briefs.md:246:| Manual tasks | Match “manual handling training” intent; lead with task-specific training and practical controls | “If your team performs manual tasks, start with the work—not a generic lifting lecture.” | Manual Handling Training hero first; explain review-to-training pathway | Operations/WHS thought leadership on task-led programmes |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/D-creative-briefs.md:247:| Care-sector manual handling — Appendix B `GOOGLE_CONV_Care-Sector_AU_2026Q3` | Dedicated sector-themed RSAs for aged-care providers, healthcare services and NDIS/disability-support organisations; qualify the buyer as an organisation planning training for teams | Not a standalone Meta launch concept. If considered later, address care-sector organisations and workplace processes only; never imply that the viewer or any individual has a disability or health condition | Care-sector module within the Manual Handling variant using aged care, healthcare and disability-support workplace language, defined team scope and supervisor follow-through; no individual credential framing | Potential named-account angle only after service scope, buyer list and LinkedIn economics are approved |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/D-creative-briefs.md:251:| Certificate / course mixed intent — Appendix B `GOOGLE_CONV_Certificate-MixedIntent_AU_2026Q3` | **Search-only**, Exact/Phrase: qualify organisational buyers and route to the gated certificate LP block. Buyer type is **UNCLASSIFIED**; do not build or publish until accreditation and participant attendance/training-completion outputs are confirmed | **N/A—excluded from Meta.** | Certificate disqualifier/reframe block; client sign-off required on whether ErgoWorks issues an accredited certificate, statement of attainment, or participant attendance/training-completion records | Not applicable |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/D-creative-briefs.md:252:| Hybrid / return-to-office | “Plan consistent office and home-work support” | “If your team works across locations, consistency needs a repeatable process.” | Hybrid variant with office/home workflow | HR and Workplace Experience ABM for return-to-office programmes |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/D-creative-briefs.md:254:| Snapshot entry offer | Match commercial searches with the dominant baseline CTA; preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis | Introduce one-issue, 15-minute B2B offer as the dominant baseline CTA with the same adjacent caveat | Make the Snapshot the dominant CTA with the same adjacent caveat | Use only for selected accounts after LinkedIn economics are validated and carry the same adjacent caveat |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/D-creative-briefs.md:255:| Individual certificate-seeker (exclude/redirect) | Google Search only: route to organic blog content — a blog post already ranks #1 for "manual handling certificate" — or to the LP certificate disqualifier block; exact individual phrasings are negative candidates (Appendix B decision table) | **N/A — do not target.** Certificate intent is never a Meta audience or creative angle | Certificate disqualifier/reframe block on the Manual Handling variant | Not applicable |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/D-creative-briefs.md:256:| Online / flexible delivery — Appendix B `GOOGLE_CONV_Online-Teams_AU_2026Q3` | **Search-only** themed RSA set: organisational framing such as “Give your team a training format that fits distributed or hybrid schedules.” The verified variants total approximately 290 searches/month (`research/keyword-research-ahrefs-2026-07-13.md` §4); never use individual credential framing | **Do not port to Meta.** It blends with individual-intent traffic, and the Meta word ban in the policy-safe messaging rules remains unchanged | Flexible online team delivery named as a module within the Manual Handling variant; qualify organisation, team scope and delivery format | Not applicable |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/D-creative-briefs.md:257:| Ongoing control / refresher — Appendix B `GOOGLE_CONV_Refresher-Teams_AU_2026Q3` | Match refresher intent with a defined team review and refresh cadence; connect to ErgoControl without implying a mandated frequency | Show the journey from one-off activity to an organised programme only after the broader baseline is established | Explain the recurring review, refresher and ErgoControl/managed-retainer pathway; cadence and outputs remain scope-dependent | Software/workflow document ad for large named accounts |
