docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:51:Initially, Meta optimises to website `Lead`, generated by valid `snapshot_request` and `direct_enquiry` events only.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:59:| Proven — 70% | Google Search | Preserve and improve mature demand capture; strengthen Manual Handling Training, care-sector, online/refresher, assessment and consultant coverage; establish Brand protection | Search already produces approximately 20 real leads per month. AU volume includes `manual handling training` at 2,700 searches/month, a care-sector cluster at approximately 780 searches/month, and a certificate/course demand head of approximately 3,400+ searches/month whose buyer type remains unclassified |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:60:| Greenfield demand-generation / TOFU pilot — target ~20% steady-state share once earned | Meta | Create demand among organisational buyers; educate, qualify and retarget traffic into the dedicated conversion landing page | Meta is greenfield for ErgoWorks. Use organisational messaging, creative qualification, interests, qualified-lead lookalikes and retargeting—not job-title targeting; it earns the ~20% share only after showing promise |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:61:| Testing — 10% | PMax plus remarketing | Evaluate incremental reach only after measurement and landing-page remediation | PMax requires at least A$50/day, or A$1,500 per 30-day planning month. A normal 10% slice is insufficient at current spend |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:64:Search remains the revenue engine. The 2026-07-13 Ahrefs AU pull confirms every volume in the account-snapshot table below exactly; these figures are verified demand indicators, not forecasts of available clicks or leads. CPC figures retain the source caveat: Ahrefs values are treated as approximate A$ planning estimates, not observed Google Ads CPCs (`research/keyword-research-ahrefs-2026-07-13.md` §1):
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:79:`ergonomic assessment software` is retained in this verification table because it was part of the original snapshot, but the verified intent is software/SaaS and it is an exclusion candidate—not a positive ErgoAssess keyword—unless later Search Terms Report evidence proves relevant consulting intent.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:85:The scenarios are anchored to both the approximately **A$40,000 trailing-12-month Search investment** and the observed **A$3.0k–A$4.7k monthly range**, using the verified last-30-day spend of **A$4,246** as the exact planning baseline.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:87:For Meta planning, the initial optimisation event is website `Lead`, generated by valid `snapshot_request` and `direct_enquiry` events only—not raw Search enquiries or soft actions. No observed Meta lead-entry CPA exists; the provisional range below is derived from the lower-friction Snapshot path and remains assumption-based:
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:89:- **Assumption 1:** a Snapshot Request costs **25%–40%** of the A$212.30 Search raw-enquiry CPL because it is a free, lower-friction lead magnet.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:91:- **Planning anchor:** use the conservative upper end, **A$84.92 per Snapshot Request**, until Meta produces clean observed data.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:92:- **Upper-bound sensitivity only:** A$212.30 remains a conservative raw-enquiry-CPL sensitivity; it is not the Meta target-CPA anchor.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:97:This scenario holds total media at the verified last-30-day spend. Meta receives its delivery floor, so the resulting mix cannot reach 70/20/10.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:101:| Google Search | A$4,246 − A$600 | **A$3,646** | **85.87%** |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:102:| Meta | A$20/day × 30 | **A$600** | **14.13%** |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:106:Decision: use only if the budget must remain flat. Meta’s A$600 budget passes both the delivery floor and the provisional A$424.60 learning-budget check for one ad set. Treat this as a controlled baseline-establishment test because the Snapshot-request CPA is assumption-based and commercial lead economics remain unknown.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:110:### Scenario 2 — Minimum-viable Meta added on top
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:112:This scenario protects the existing Search run-rate and adds the Meta delivery floor, which is higher than the provisional learning-budget requirement.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:116:| Google Search | Existing last-30-day baseline | **A$4,246.00** | **87.62%** |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:117:| Meta | Higher of A$600 delivery floor and 5 × A$84.92 | **A$600.00** | **12.38%** |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:121:Decision: preferred minimum launch scenario. It protects the existing Search run-rate while funding one Meta ad set above both sufficiency checks. It does not achieve the intended 80/20 active-channel mix; that overlay should not override the current event-level planning assumptions or platform floor.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:123:Meta receives **A$20/day** over 30 days. Keep this in one consolidated prospecting ad set initially. Build retargeting audiences but do not fragment the budget.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:125:### Scenario 3 — Minimum-viable Meta plus PMax at its floor
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:127:This scenario keeps the existing Search baseline, adds minimum-viable Meta and funds PMax at A$50/day.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:131:| Google Search | Existing last-30-day baseline | **A$4,246.00** | **66.91%** |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:132:| Meta | Higher of A$600 delivery floor and 5 × A$84.92 | **A$600.00** | **9.45%** |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:137:Decision: use only after the measurement and landing-page gates pass. Platform floors materially override 70/20/10: PMax becomes 23.64% rather than 10%, while Search is 66.91% and Meta is 9.45%.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:145:| Meta delivery floor | A$20/day × 30 | A$600 per 30-day planning period per ad set | Scenarios 1–3 pass with one ad set |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:146:| Raw Search enquiry CPL | A$4,246 last-30-day Search spend ÷ approximately 20 real leads | A$212.30 | Conservative upper-bound sensitivity only—not the Meta target-CPA anchor |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:147:| Assumed Snapshot-request CPA range | A$212.30 × assumed 25%–40% lower-friction-event factor | A$53.08–A$84.92 | Assumption-based pending clean Meta Snapshot-request data |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:148:| Provisional Meta target CPA | Conservative upper end of assumed Snapshot-request CPA range | A$84.92 | Planning anchor only—not a qualified-lead or profitable-acquisition target |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:149:| Meta learning budget | 5 × A$84.92 | A$424.60 per 30-day planning period per ad set | Scenarios 1–3 pass with one ad set; A$600 delivery floor is controlling |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:150:| Raw-enquiry-CPL upper-bound sensitivity | 5 × A$212.30 | A$1,061.50 per 30-day planning period per ad set | Sensitivity only; not used to set the proposed Meta budgets |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:155:The A$84.92 figure is an assumption-labeled event-level planning anchor, not a commercially defensible target CPA. The A$212.30 raw-enquiry CPL is retained only as an upper-bound sensitivity. A further caveat on the derivation: the "approximately 20 real leads" denominator is undifferentiated and may include certificate-intent conversions — "manual handling certificate" alone drew 55 clicks / 1.67 conversions in the last 30 days (`research/live-evidence-2026-07-12.md`) and those conversions are unclassified as individual versus organisational — so both A$212.30 and the derived A$84.92 anchor could be understated as costs per genuine corporate lead. Average contract value, contribution margin, qualified-lead rate, close rate and service capacity are unknown. Until those inputs and a clean conversion baseline exist:
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:159:- assess provisional Meta learning sufficiency against website `Lead`, while labelling A$84.92 as a Snapshot-path planning assumption rather than a blended observed CPA;
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:160:- replace the assumed range with observed Snapshot-request CPA as soon as clean Meta data is available;
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:171:| Measurement | Inventory all 16 enabled conversion actions; isolate Consulting goals; demote newsletter and inappropriate soft actions; document browser/server deduplication; define `snapshot_request`, `direct_enquiry`, `call_connected`, `qualified_call`, `lead_qualified`, `proposal_sent` and `closed_won`; keep Snapshot booked/held as CRM stages, not platform events | 100% of active Consulting campaigns mapped to an approved conversion-goal set; zero newsletter signups used as primary Consulting optimisation events; test submissions reconcile across landing page, CRM, GA4 and ad platforms |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:172:| Privacy | Implement CMP requirements and **Consent Mode v2, default denied, with no client- or server-side analytics/advertising transmission before consent**; keep separate marketing consent; complete AU privacy review | Privacy review approved before paid-social or new landing-page launch; no health or injury fields in advertising forms |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:173:| Landing page | Prepare a dedicated, navigation-reduced page with a two-step form and message-matched variants | One primary CTA per variant; all ads mapped to the intended variant; form validation and consent states pass QA |
