docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:175:| Meta | Create isolated Pixel/Dataset scope, audiences and one consolidated prospecting build; creative specifications remain in Appendix D | Browser/server event deduplication test passes; audience exclusions and domain scope documented; campaign remains unpublished until privacy and tracking gates pass |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:182:| Search | Launch approved landing-page routing and tightly themed Exact/Phrase coverage; retain Maximize Conversions while the clean baseline forms | 100% of paid Search destinations use approved, relevant pages; weekly search-term review completed; no known product or physio bleed left unclassified |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:183:| Meta | Launch one consolidated website-lead prospecting ad set under Scenario 1 or 2. Initially, Meta optimises to website `Lead`, generated by valid `snapshot_request` and `direct_enquiry` events only. Enable Advantage+ placements; build visitor and engagement pools | Minimum A$20/day delivered; at least three materially distinct formats and five creatives available in the ad set, subject to Appendix D; Meta delivery, CTR, form-start and lead-entry CPA baselines recorded without declaring winners prematurely |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:185:| Governance | Review copy and form behaviour against AU and Meta policy | Every Snapshot placement includes “preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis”; zero personal-condition messaging |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:191:| Search diagnosis | Compare clusters by query relevance, landing-page engagement, real-lead mix and emerging qualified-lead signals | Every active cluster assigned a diagnosis flag: retain, repair, insufficient data or candidate test; no unconditional kill/scale label without thresholds |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:192:| Meta diagnosis | Compare creative concepts and audience delivery without fragmenting budget | Creative fatigue and format coverage reviewed; prospecting frequency maintained below 3.0 over seven days where reporting permits; audience overlap reviewed before adding ad sets |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:200:| CPA greater than 3× an approved target | At least seven days and 20 clicks | Flag for pause review; inspect query intent, tracking, landing page and lead quality first |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:203:| Meta prospecting frequency | Seven-day frequency 3–5 | Warning; inspect audience size and creative fatigue |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:204:| Meta prospecting frequency | Seven-day frequency above 5 | Fail diagnosis; do not assume budget alone is the cause |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:206:| Search Quality Score | 5–6 warning; below 5 fail | Diagnose relevance, expected CTR and landing-page experience |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:207:| Search CTR | At least 6.66% pass; 3–6.66% warning; below 3% fail | Apply only after comparable, clean campaign segmentation |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:208:| Search CVR | At least 7.52% pass; 3–7.52% warning; below 3% fail | Use real primary conversions, not the current blended 26 |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:209:| Search CPC | Up to A$5.26 pass; A$5.26–A$8 warning; above A$8 fail | Diagnose by keyword intent and qualified-lead value |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:215:These ranges are planning scenarios, not commitments. They assume the dedicated landing page launches, measurement is corrected, Meta receives adequate creative, privacy approval is obtained, service capacity is available, and budgets follow one of the proposed scenarios.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:219:| Months 1–3 | Search and Meta measurement baselines established; PMax parked | Scenario 2 launches with Search protected and Meta funded at A$600 per 30 days | Scenario 2 prepares PMax readiness while qualified-lead feedback begins |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:220:| Months 4–6 | Search remains dominant; Meta continues only if delivery and lead-quality signals are interpretable | Meta receives up to 20% increases only after stable evidence; qualified-lead imports guide allocation | Scenario 3 activates PMax at A$1,500 per 30 days after all gates pass |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:221:| Months 7–9 | Budget remains within the approved envelope informed by the A$3.0k–A$4.7k observed range; focus stays on efficiency and de-mixing | Total media operates around A$4,846 per 30 days, subject to commercial approval | Total media starts around A$6,346 per 30 days; PMax incrementality is tested against Search and Meta |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:222:| Months 10–12 | PMax and paid remarketing remain parked if qualified-lead evidence is weak | Search/Meta allocation moves according to observed Snapshot-request and qualified-lead economics, subject to each ad set’s delivery and learning floors | Search/Meta/PMax allocation moves according to observed qualified-pipeline economics, subject to platform floors and incrementality evidence |
