docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:274:Each keyword below enters only in Exact and Phrase; no Broad launch rows. Volumes are Australian average monthly searches from the verified 2026-07-13 Ahrefs pull. A dash means Ahrefs did not report that field in the source—not zero (`research/keyword-research-ahrefs-2026-07-13.md` §§3–4).
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:276:The CPC figures in this standalone table are approximate Ahrefs planning inputs, **not observed Google Ads CPC**.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:280:| `GOOGLE_CONV_Care-Sector_AU_2026Q3` | `[manual handling training for aged care workers]` | `"manual handling training for aged care workers"` | 150 | 15 | — |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:287:| `GOOGLE_CONV_Online-Teams_AU_2026Q3` | `[manual handling training online]` | `"manual handling training online"` | 150 | — | — |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:290:| `GOOGLE_CONV_Refresher-Teams_AU_2026Q3` | `[manual handling refresher training]` | `"manual handling refresher training"` | 100 | — | — |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:293:The care-sector set totals approximately **780 searches/month** before close-variant overlap, with low KD on several terms and unambiguously organisational buyer language. This is the cleanest corporate-fit cluster in the verified dataset. The online set totals approximately **290 searches/month** and remains Search-only. The refresher set totals approximately **160 searches/month** and is a recurring-purchase signal, not evidence of a mandated cadence; any cadence or recurring-service claim remains scope- and client-sign-off-dependent.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:295:**Care-sector negative-conflict launch blocker:** the live 419 campaign-level negative list currently contains `"aged care"` PHRASE, `disability` BROAD, `"health care"` PHRASE, `healthcare` BROAD and multiple exact/phrase healthcare-training exclusions. Those controls would block much of this new ad group. Before publication, reconcile and remove or narrow every conflicting negative after confirming service scope; do not publish the group while the conflict remains (`research/live-keywords-negatives-2026-07-12.md`).
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:304:| `manual handling training near me` | 350 | Exact + Phrase candidate only when location targeting uses Presence and the landing page can truthfully resolve service coverage |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:311:City-level bid modifiers still require the Google geo-performance report. Do not infer modifiers from Ahrefs volume or from national Search Terms Report appearances, and do not make a geo scale decision until conversion goals are clean and qualified-lead location data is available (`research/keyword-research-ahrefs-2026-07-13.md` §§4, 6 and “Not verified / remaining”).
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:315:The CPC figures in this standalone table are approximate Ahrefs planning inputs, **not observed Google Ads CPC**.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:320:| `ergonomic assessment melbourne` | 150 | 0 | **A$7.00** | Commercial + transactional; Geo group and dedicated assessment landing-page variant |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:321:| `ergonomic assessment sydney` | 100 | 0 | **A$6.00** | Commercial geo intent; Geo group and dedicated assessment landing-page variant |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:327:Sydney and Melbourne are high-value but pricey assessment terms. Their A$6.00/A$7.00 Ahrefs CPC estimates justify tight Exact/Phrase structure and close search-term review, not an unconditional manual bid or scale instruction. Pair them with the dedicated assessment landing-page variant and qualified-lead measurement before any budget increase. All scale and bid-strategy changes remain conditional on a clean conversion baseline (`research/keyword-research-ahrefs-2026-07-13.md` §5).
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:331:Additional commercial modifiers such as `corporate`, `workplace`, `for employees`, `onsite` and `Australia` remain proposed hypotheses. The city and near-me volumes in the coverage sheet are Ahrefs-verified; they need service-coverage approval and Google geo-performance evidence, not volume re-verification, before publication or bid modification.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:344:| Landing pages | Dedicated, message-matched page variant; no routing to ErgoEquip, Physiotherapy or unrelated pages |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:350:A large negative inventory already exists: **419 campaign-level plus 74 ad-group-level negatives on campaign 700072710** (`research/live-keywords-negatives-2026-07-12.md`). The task is therefore not building a list from scratch but **auditing the existing 493 negatives** for overblocking, staleness (many single-name/person negatives suggest long accumulation) and gaps around the confirmed waste terms (certificate-intent and regulator queries from the 2026-07-12 search-terms pull).
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:352:New candidates must be validated against actual Search Terms Reports. Use Exact negatives for specific irrelevant searches and Phrase negatives for clearly irrelevant intent patterns. Do not use speculative broad-match negatives.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:363:| CPR / first-aid bundle — conditional | `"cpr"` only if ErgoWorks confirms it does not deliver or partner on CPR; retain/review the existing `"first aid"` PHRASE and `[first aid and manual handling training]` EXACT controls rather than duplicating them | Ahrefs shows bundled demand at 150/month for `manual handling and cpr training` and 70/month for `manual handling and first aid training`, but keyword research is not a Search Terms Report. Hold any new negative until service scope is confirmed and an actual irrelevant query validates the match type |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:364:| Vehicle ergonomics | `[driver ergonomic assessment]` if an actual irrelevant query appears; no duplicate additions for car/vehicle terms | The legacy list already has `car` BROAD, `[car ergonomic assessment]` EXACT and `[vehicle ergonomic assessment]` EXACT. Audit the over-broad `car` control and retain or narrow the exact controls; Ahrefs identifies car/vehicle/driver tails at 40/40/30 searches/month as out of scope |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:365:| Assessment software / SaaS | `[ergonomic assessment software]` as the narrow candidate after Search Terms Report confirmation | The verified term has 40 searches/month and SaaS intent. Existing controls include `app` BROAD and several software-specific negatives, but not this exact phrase; audit the broad controls for overblocking and do not run this term as a positive ErgoAssess keyword |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:366:| Free manual-handling variants | No duplicate addition while `free` BROAD remains live; after the audit, replace or retain only evidence-backed Exact/Phrase controls such as `[manual handling course free]` and specific `"free online"` query patterns | The campaign already has `free` BROAD and `[manual handling course free]` EXACT. Because Broad negatives can overblock and the approved Snapshot itself uses “free,” audit routing and duplication before any change; source any replacement from actual irrelevant Search Terms Report queries |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:372:“Manual handling certificate” is the largest single search term by spend in the **2026-07-12 30-day top-60 pull** (A$364.86 / 55 clicks / 1.67 conv ≈ 3% CVR, versus “manual handling training” at ~13.6%), but certificate queries are not uniformly waste: “manual handling certificate online australia” produced **1.33 conversions from A$15.92**. The buyer type remains **UNCLASSIFIED** in current conversion data.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:374:Ahrefs now verifies that this is a large demand pool rather than a fringe tail (`research/keyword-research-ahrefs-2026-07-13.md` §2). The CPC figures below are approximate Ahrefs planning inputs, **not observed Google Ads CPC**:
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:380:| `manual handling certificate online` | **150** | 43 | A$1.30 | Mixed online/certificate intent; Search-only and organisational qualification required |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:383:The certificate + course head alone is approximately **3,400 searches/month**, with another 210/month across the verified online-certificate and accredited terms before close-variant overlap. This strengthens Option A because it tests a material pool, but volume does not classify the buyer as organisational. Do not blanket-exclude. Use these complementary controls as evidence permits:
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:387:| **A — dedicated Certificate / Course mixed-intent split (RECOMMENDED, gated trial)** | Build as `GOOGLE_CONV_Certificate-MixedIntent_AU_2026Q3`, Search-only, using Exact + Phrase and organisational qualification; route to the Manual Handling variant's certificate block. Do not build or publish until the client confirms whether ErgoWorks issues an accredited certificate, statement of attainment, or participant attendance/training-completion records | The verified approximately 3,400+ search/month pool makes the trial material rather than fringe, but buyer type remains **UNCLASSIFIED**. **Gated on the LP certificate block, accreditation and participant-record evidence, and client sign-off** (Appendix A); excluded from Meta |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:388:| **B — exact-negative individual phrasings (can coexist with A)** | Exact negatives only on clearly individual searches such as personal-validity, personal-card or individual-accreditation phrasings; rely on the existing #1 organic blog ranking for excluded individual demand | Blocks only the exact clearly individual queries selected; it does not block broader corporate/online certificate queries unless those exact converting phrases are added in error |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:390:“Accredited manual handling training” at **60 searches/month** makes accreditation a keyword-visible product question. ErgoWorks must confirm whether it provides accredited training, a statement of attainment, or participant attendance/training-completion records before the term, claim or landing-page block can publish; absent that evidence, do not bid on accreditation intent and do not imply equivalence. In either option, **Meta never targets certificate intent** (see Appendix D).
