docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:3:> **Scope:** Snapshot-based diagnostic plan for ErgoWorks Consulting, not a completed Google Ads audit. It uses verified account data as at 12 July 2026, including last-30-day search terms, the full keyword/status/match-type/headline-Quality-Score inventory and 493 negatives. A full audit still requires longer history, RSAs/assets, complete campaign settings, Quality Score components and geo/device performance reports. No live-account changes are authorised by this plan.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:7:This is an optimisation plan for a mature Search program, not a greenfield launch.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:11:| Google Ads account | **9258098368** — “zzz Ergoworks” |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:13:| Focus campaign | **700072710** — Ergoworks Consulting Search |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:22:| Missing growth layers | No paid Meta activity; no dedicated conversion landing page; paused PMax and remarketing |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:23:| Evidence limitation | Search terms (30-day), keyword/match-type/status/headline-Quality-Score inventory, 493 negatives and a partial geo signal were pulled 2026-07-12 (`research/live-evidence-2026-07-12.md`, `research/live-keywords-negatives-2026-07-12.md`); still missing: longer performance history, negative-list audit, RSA/asset inventory, complete campaign settings, Quality Score components and geo/device performance reports |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:42:| Conversion stage | Definition | Google Ads treatment |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:64:Duration is a screening condition, not proof of qualification. The CRM/call-tracking disposition is authoritative. The exact duration and operating-hours rule remains **awaiting client approval**. Keep any native duration-based proxy **Secondary**. Import `qualified_call` as the only Primary call signal using a stable order ID derived from the CRM opportunity/call record. If a proxy was previously imported in error, retract or restate it with Google Ads conversion adjustments before the qualified import; never count the proxy and qualified import as two conversions for the same call.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:75:8. Reconcile Google Ads, GA4 and CRM totals before treating the new baseline as clean.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:82:Before new forms, remarketing audiences or server-side signals go live:
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:85:- Do not collect injury details, symptoms, diagnoses or other health information in advertising forms.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:86:- Implement an appropriate CMP and **Consent Mode v2, default denied, with no client- or server-side analytics/advertising transmission before consent**.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:87:- Complete an Australian privacy review covering GA4, GTM, CRM, Google Ads, Meta Pixel and CAPI.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:89:- Use only controllable-output claims; do not claim guaranteed injury prevention, assured WHS compliance or quantified claims reductions.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:114:The synthesis, however, concludes that **Maximize Conversions is the practical ceiling at approximately 20 real conversions/month**. The live campaign also has established Search history rather than being a new campaign.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:116:This conflict should not be resolved by automatically switching a mature campaign to Maximize Clicks. Maximize Clicks optimises traffic volume rather than lead quality and could amplify irrelevant demand before the resolved 30-day search-term evidence and existing 493-negative inventory have been fully audited and extended with longer history.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:122:| Fewer than 20 clean primary conversions/month, weak or unstable delivery, and no reliable qualified-lead imports | Test whether Maximize Clicks with a benchmark-based CPC cap can rebuild usable volume, but only after search terms and negatives are reviewed |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:130:A CPC cap cannot be responsibly prescribed from the snapshot because keyword-level CPC/performance history and longer-term query distributions were not supplied, although match types and headline Quality Scores are resolved. It should be based on the extended keyword and search-term performance export, not the generic Search benchmark.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:136:Manual Handling Training consumed **A$2,069**, or **49% of the A$4,246 last-30-day spend**. This concentration is directionally plausible because “manual handling training” is the dominant verified demand term at approximately 2,700 Australian searches per month. Concentration alone is not proof of waste.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:155:| Clean CPA is above T but below 3T | At least 14 days and at least 20 clicks | Diagnose search terms, match types, ads, landing page and lead quality before changing budget |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:163:Separately, the "DSA - Ergoworks Consulting" ad group spent **A$795 in the last 30 days (18.7% of spend, 55 clicks, 4.5 reported conversions)**. Conversion quality for that group total is unverified. The live keyword pull shows it is not a Dynamic Search Ads group: it holds nine static EXACT keywords—six competitor-keyword entries across four competitors plus three generics. Only the sampled government/competitor-query subset was near-zero converting. Its evidence gap is therefore not "DSA settings and final URLs" but whether the group-level 4.5 reported conversions represent qualified demand and whether the sampled leakage warrants tighter query controls (see Appendix B reclassification).
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:172:| CPA at or below T but impression share is constrained by rank | Improve relevance, ads, landing page and Quality Score before adding budget |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:181:The Brand ad group inside campaign 700072710 delivered **A$0 spend, zero clicks and zero conversions in the last 30 days**. Dedicated Brand routing and reporting are absent; service groups currently capture Brand queries.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:185:The 2026-07-12 keyword pull (`research/live-keywords-negatives-2026-07-12.md`, §Brand) confirms the sole diagnosed cause: **all three Brand keywords — "ergoworks" PHRASE, "ergoworks" EXACT and "ergoworks physio" PHRASE — are PAUSED** (QS=None). No ineligibility, budget-starvation or negative-blocking investigation is required to explain the zero delivery.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:187:The same pull adds a structural refinement: **all three terms—"ergoworks" PHRASE, "ergoworks" EXACT and "ergoworks physio" PHRASE—are ENABLED as duplicates inside five non-brand ad groups** (Manual Handling Training, Ergonomic Office Consulting, Ergonomics Assessments, Workplace Ergonomics, School Ergonomics). Brand queries are therefore not unprotected — they are being captured by whichever service ad group wins the internal auction, served non-brand ads and non-brand landing pages, and reported inside service ad-group metrics. The repair is consolidation, not just re-enablement: remove all three duplicated terms from the five service ad groups when the Brand ad group is re-enabled, so brand traffic routes to dedicated brand ads and its spend/conversion contribution to the service groups' reported performance is unwound (a small portion of Manual Handling Training's reported conversions may currently be brand-query conversions).
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:202:| Brand has meaningful impressions but loses share to budget or rank, or requires different bidding, budget, reporting, negatives or messaging | Break Brand into its own always-on Search campaign |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:204:| There is no measurable brand search demand after eligibility is confirmed | Retain a minimal eligible structure and monitor; do not force spend |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:207:Once delivery resumes, pull brand search volume, search terms, auction insights, impression share and lost impression share by budget/rank before deciding repair-in-place versus campaign breakout.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:233:| **GO — fund to floor** | Incremental or deliberately reallocated budget of at least A$1,500 per 30 days; clean primary conversions; qualified-lead import operating; dedicated Consulting landing page; verified asset set; brand exclusions; campaign-level negatives; URL expansion controls; audience signals; separate Consulting measurement scope |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:235:| **NO-GO pending audit** | Existing PMax asset groups, URLs, brand exclusions, negatives, search themes, historical search categories or conversion settings reveal cross-business contamination |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:237:**Recommendation: PARK PMax unless it can be funded to at least A$50/day without destabilising proven Search.** Do not reactivate it merely to satisfy a nominal 10% testing allocation.
