docs/ergoworks-consulting/ergoworks-campaign-plan.md:66:### Search concentration
docs/ergoworks-consulting/ergoworks-campaign-plan.md:68:Manual Handling Training received **A$2,069—49% of the A$4,246 last-30-day spend**. Manual handling training remains the current spend anchor and largest verified **TRAINING** term at **2,700 Australian searches per month**; research also identifies an approximately **3,400-searches-per-month mixed-intent certificate/course pool** with buyer type **UNCLASSIFIED** and an approximately **780-searches-per-month care-sector opportunity**. These are directional demand estimates, not forecasts or verified service fit, and both expansion pockets remain gated as set out in Appendices A–D.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/ergoworks-campaign-plan.md:79:| Brand | A$0 | 0 | All three dedicated Brand terms are paused; the same three terms are duplicated across five service groups, so repair requires in-place re-enablement and de-duplication before any breakout decision |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/ergoworks-campaign-plan.md:81:Paid traffic currently lands on generic WordPress pages, led by the Manual Handling Training page with 234 clicks in the last 30 days. There is no dedicated paid-media conversion page.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/ergoworks-campaign-plan.md:85:The available evidence includes last-30-day search terms, the full keyword inventory with match types, statuses and headline Quality Scores, 493 negatives and a partial geography signal. Remaining gaps are longer search-term and keyword-performance history, the negative-list audit, RSAs/assets, complete campaign settings, Quality Score components and geo/device performance reports. Consequently, the package supports a diagnostic plan—not unconditional pause, restructure or scale instructions.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/ergoworks-campaign-plan.md:99:The promise is controllable outputs—not guaranteed injury prevention, assured WHS compliance, claims reductions or medical outcomes.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/ergoworks-campaign-plan.md:117:All budgets use a **30-day planning period**. They are anchored to both the approximately **A$40,000 trailing-12-month Search investment** and the observed **A$3.0k–A$4.7k monthly range**, with the verified **A$4,246 last-30-day spend** as the exact planning baseline.
