docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/C-tracking-spec.md:27:### Proposed Google Ads conversion treatment
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/C-tracking-spec.md:29:| Action | Google treatment | Count setting | Reason |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/C-tracking-spec.md:45:Use Google Ads native conversion actions as the bidding source where technically appropriate. Keep equivalent GA4 key events for analysis and observation only. Do not count both a GA4-imported event and a native Google Ads action for the same conversion.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/C-tracking-spec.md:53:Duration is a screening condition, not proof of qualification. The CRM/call-tracking disposition is authoritative. The exact duration and operating-hours rule remains **awaiting client approval**. Keep any native duration-based proxy **Secondary**. Import `qualified_call` as the only Primary call signal using a stable order ID derived from the CRM opportunity/call record. If a proxy was previously imported in error, retract or restate it with Google Ads conversion adjustments before the qualified import; never count the proxy and qualified import as two conversions for the same call.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/C-tracking-spec.md:71:| Funnel stage | Canonical event | Source of truth | Google bidding treatment | Meta bidding treatment |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/C-tracking-spec.md:76:| Qualified call | `qualified_call` | CRM/call disposition applying W-Audit rule | Primary only via qualified import once reliable | Send through CAPI; optimisation only after reliable volume |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/C-tracking-spec.md:78:| Proposal | `proposal_sent` | CRM stage | Secondary | CAPI reporting/custom audience |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/C-tracking-spec.md:79:| Won | `closed_won` | CRM finance-approved stage | Value-bearing secondary initially | CAPI value event and audience exclusion |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/C-tracking-spec.md:85:- Google campaign 700072710 continues with Maximize Conversions and no tCPA, bidding only to cleaned Snapshot requests, direct enquiries and qualified calls.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/C-tracking-spec.md:86:- Initially, Meta optimises to website `Lead`, generated by valid `snapshot_request` and `direct_enquiry` events only.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/C-tracking-spec.md:93:- Move Google’s campaign-specific goal toward `lead_qualified` only after the event is deduplicated, timely, consistently defined and producing at least **30 clean qualified conversions per month** for a stable evaluation period. Until then, tCPA/tROAS remains premature.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/C-tracking-spec.md:94:- Move Meta toward CRM-qualified-lead optimisation only after the event is arriving reliably, match quality is acceptable, and volume is sufficient for stable delivery. Do not force a fixed threshold before Meta’s actual learning diagnostics and the qualified-lead baseline are known.
