docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md-60-The final rule must be identical to the definition adopted in Appendix C. Until that rule is approved, use this proposed implementation hook:
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md-61-
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:62:> **Awaiting client approval:** a qualified call is a unique inbound call attributable to ErgoWorks Consulting that reaches a human or approved call-handling service, meets the approved minimum connected-duration and operating-hours conditions, and is dispositioned as a legitimate B2B workplace-ergonomics enquiry. It must exclude spam, wrong numbers, job seekers, suppliers, consumer equipment-shopping enquiries, Physiotherapy, clinical or personal-health enquiries, and repeat calls about the same opportunity.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md-63-
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:64:Duration is a screening condition, not proof of qualification. The CRM/call-tracking disposition is authoritative. The exact duration and operating-hours rule remains **awaiting client approval**. Keep any native duration-based proxy **Secondary**. Import `qualified_call` as the only Primary call signal using a stable order ID derived from the CRM opportunity/call record. If a proxy was previously imported in error, retract or restate it with Google Ads conversion adjustments before the qualified import; never count the proxy and qualified import as two conversions for the same call.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md-65-
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md-66-### Required conversion-cleanup sequence
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md-67-
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:68:1. Inventory all **16 enabled conversion actions**, their source, category, counting method, attribution, lookback window, campaign-goal inclusion and owning business.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:69:2. Define a campaign-specific Consulting goal set for campaign 700072710.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:70:3. Remove Physiotherapy conversion actions from the Consulting campaign’s optimisation scope. Do not apply account-wide exclusions or negatives that could damage the separate Physiotherapy campaign.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:71:4. Demote Newsletter Sign Up, Email Click, Call Forwarding, clicks-to-call and local/soft actions from primary to secondary.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md-72-5. Validate Make an Enquiry against actual form submissions and exclude spam, tests and duplicates.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md-73-6. Implement the qualified-call rule and document how call disposition is recorded.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md-74-7. Add offline imports for qualified lead, proposal and closed-won stages using stable click identifiers and CRM records.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md-75-8. Reconcile Google Ads, GA4 and CRM totals before treating the new baseline as clean.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md-76-9. Preserve historical annotations so the reporting discontinuity is visible.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md-77-
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:78:Changing primary conversions will change Smart Bidding behaviour and reported CPA. Expect a learning and restabilisation period; do not interpret an immediate fall in reported conversions as lost business when easy actions have deliberately been removed.
