    77	
    78	| Stage | Offer | Eligibility / best fit | Exact deliverable and pricing status | Required caveat |
    79	|---|---|---|---|---|
    80	| Entry | **Free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot** | B2B organisational buyer with one defined workplace-ergonomics question; capacity and service geography must be approved | 15-minute consultant conversation and written three-point summary; free, subject to approved fulfilment capacity | Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis |
    81	| Paid entry | **ErgoStart** | Defined site, cohort or issue | Fixed-scope assessment sprint and prioritised actions; pricing unconfirmed and must not be advertised until client-approved | Scope, inclusions, delivery timing and price are confirmed only in an approved proposal |
    82	| Rollout | **ErgoScale** | Corporate, multi-site or hybrid programme | Repeatable workflow, implementation plan and reporting; pricing unconfirmed | Coverage, timing and outputs depend on the approved programme scope |
    83	| Capability | **ErgoCoach** | Manual-task or train-the-trainer need | Task-led review, tailored training and supervisor toolkit; pricing unconfirmed | Format, participants and outputs depend on the approved scope |
    84	| Ongoing | **ErgoControl** | Organisation requiring ongoing programme visibility | ErgoAssess subscription or managed retainer, review cadence and reporting; pricing unconfirmed | Platform, service level, cadence and outputs depend on the approved scope |
    85	
    86	The Snapshot gives cold prospects a concrete next step without asking them to commit immediately to a full programme. The offer names, eligibility, fulfilment promise and ladder remain **client sign-off required**.
    87	
    88	### Primary lead magnet: Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot
    89	
    90	#### Standard offer description
   224	2. **Strategic reframe:** Start with the task, not a generic training lecture.
   225	3. **Broader pathway:** Workstation, hybrid-work and workplace-ergonomics priorities.
